{
  "id": {
    "address": "miso",
    "name": "disc"
  },
  "doc": " Represents a disc within a release, containing an ordered list of tracks.\n Multi-disc releases (like double albums) are modeled as multiple Disc objects.\n\n A disc is a pure partition of the release's tracklist — it carries no name\n of its own. A disc title (\"Disc 2: Live at Budokan\") is presentation with\n more than one correct rendering, so it lives in the metadata extension on\n the release, like all display data. Note the digest consequence: the\n release digest commits to the flattened track order, not to where disc\n boundaries fall (see `release`'s module docs on consent scope).\n\n Artwork is intentionally NOT part of core: it is display metadata whose\n format evolves over time (static → animated → future formats), so it lives\n in the `cover_art` extension on the release (an album-level cover plus\n per-track overrides) rather than frozen in an immutable struct here.",
